From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:52:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: bring the J604 panel back onto
 Aurora's display driver

The J604 series was rebuilt on integration/aurora taking Aurora's
display driver whole (2d2ca1559a), which left the J604 panel without
the work the series had on it: the 120 Hz swap timing and pacing, 10-bit
XRGB/ARGB2101010 frames, BT.2020 wide-gamut SDR, the panel EDID (Display
P3, luminances, the 24-120 Hz range), adaptive sync, the 600 nits user
maximum with the XDR guard and thermal cap, EDR, and the display power
gate while blanked.

Aurora changed the M4 files only by the 120 Hz presentation deadline
(09986eed10) since the series' base, so take the series' M4 files
(iomfb_m4, the dcp-m4 headers, the panel ADT and EDID code, plane,
backlight) and apply its changes to the shared files on top of Aurora's:
the VRR atomic check, EDR on the T8132 eDP connector, the fixed refresh
rates and the flip event stamped with the swap's completion in dcp.c,
and the panel's bright-surroundings maximum and thermal cap in the ADT
parser. The series' swap timing words do what the deadline does, so the
deadline is not sent twice.

Aurora's sleep paths, its v27 firmware support, the display fabric and
the external audio and HDMI code stay Aurora's. A T8132 dcpext's HDMI
port and idle release are not run by this driver yet: the panel path's
kicks for them are empty until they are ported.

Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 02139640ad73846fb6ea5534e6fe73a3d91299a7)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
