+/*
+ * swap_pace: internal-panel swaps carry "as soon as possible" timing words,
+ * so the panel shows a frame at the first 4.17 ms tick it can make. Measured
+ * from the last completion, even ticks are the 120 Hz grid and odd ones fall
+ * between two refreshes. A swap started now can make every tick at least the
+ * lead ahead (swap_pace_lead_us, or the learned floor). Pick the first grid
+ * tick it makes with a quarter tick to spare, and start only once the tick
+ * before it is out of reach by a quarter tick too, so that an error of up
+ * to a quarter tick in the lead still lands the frame on the grid. Returns
+ * the wait in us (less than one tick).
